# whazzon — the harvest mailbox
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so never
# put a real password here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# This is the only secret the project has. Every other stage reads committed
# files or public pages, which is why anyone who clones the repo can re-run the
# pipeline. Only `npm run mail` reads this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setting up the address (Gmail)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Use a dedicated account, not a personal one. It exists to be subscribed to
# fifty mailing lists and to be read by a script, and both of those are reasons
# not to point it at post that matters.
#
#   1. Create the account
#   2. Turn on 2-Step Verification — App Passwords are not offered without it
#        https://myaccount.google.com/signinoptions/twosv
#   3. Create an App Password ("Mail" / "Other")
#        https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#      Google shows 16 characters in four groups. Paste it below with or
#      without the spaces; both are accepted.
#   4. Check IMAP is enabled: Gmail → Settings → Forwarding and POP/IMAP
#
# The app password is a full-access credential for that mailbox, which is a
# further reason the account should hold nothing else.
#
# Then go and subscribe. The catalogue is the worklist: `npm run mail` reports
# every sender it could not attribute, so subscribing first and binding after
# is the intended order — sign up to whatever looks useful, run the pull, and
# add a `mail:` block to the sources it names.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here is Gmail-specific
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It is plain IMAP, so Fastmail, Proton Bridge or a self-hosted server work by
# changing the host. That is deliberate: binding the project to one provider's
# API for a protocol that has been stable for thirty years would be a poor
# trade, and the Gmail API needs a Cloud project and an OAuth consent screen to
# do the same job.

WHAZZON_MAIL_HOST=imap.gmail.com
WHAZZON_MAIL_PORT=993
WHAZZON_MAIL_USER=
WHAZZON_MAIL_PASS="xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx"

# Which mailbox to read. INBOX is the sensible default. If you filter each
# subscription into a Gmail label, name the label here instead — a label is an
# IMAP mailbox, and nested ones are "parent/child".
WHAZZON_MAIL_MAILBOX=INBOX

# How far back a pull looks when `--since` is not given. Overlapping windows
# cost nothing: messages already filed are recognised by Message-Id and
# skipped, so err on the generous side.
WHAZZON_MAIL_SINCE_DAYS=14

# Senders never worth filing: the mailbox provider's own service mail. Comma
# separated, same glob syntax as a catalogue `mail:` binding. Unset uses the
# built-in list (Google account notices, bounce daemons). Set it to override,
# not to add — the built-in list is replaced, not extended.
# WHAZZON_MAIL_IGNORE=*@accounts.google.com,*@google.com,mailer-daemon@*,postmaster@*
